struct S { int g(); };
S f(int);
int a();
void h() { 0; }

// Regression test: the two calls in `f(...).g()` begin at the same offset, so
// rewriting the outer one invalidates the source range of the inner one.
// Rewriter::getRangeSize() then maps the inner range's end below its own
// beginning and returns a negative size, which used to be passed to
// Rewriter::ReplaceText() as an `unsigned` length. The argument list is long
// enough that the resulting offsets fall outside the buffer, so RewriteBuffer
// walked off its rope and clang_delta died with SIGSEGV. The comment is kept
// below the code on purpose: text in front of `f` would push its offset up and
// stop the range from underflowing.
